The standard library here has no wide characters, so neither does toml++

`oops-deps/libcxx` is built with `_LIBCPP_HAS_WIDE_CHARACTERS 0`: `std::wstring`
and `std::wstring_view` do not exist, and `<wchar.h>` omits the functions they
would need. toml++ already has a switch for the feature that uses them -
`TOML_ENABLE_WINDOWS_COMPAT`, off here because this is not Windows - but two
places name the types outside it.

**The `is_wide_string` trait.** Its definition names `std::wstring_view` and
`std::wstring` unconditionally, although every *use* of it is behind
`TOML_ENABLE_WINDOWS_COMPAT` (`make_node.hpp:45`, `node_view.hpp:490` and the
comparison operators beside them, each a `static_assert` saying a wide string is
not accepted without the switch). With the switch off the trait is false for
every type that reaches it, so that is what it is defined as.

**The `std::wstring` arm of `value::get()`.** `if constexpr` discards the branch
but the type still has to be declared for the condition to be written, so the
arm itself moves inside the switch rather than its body. The `static_assert`
that stood in the `#else` goes with it: an unreachable branch cannot be reached,
and the arm no longer exists to reach.

Turning wide characters on in libc++ instead is the other way to fix this, and a
larger one: it wants `wmemcpy`, `wcslen`, `mbrtowc`, `wcsrtombs` and the rest
from the C library, and a libc++ that compiles and then fails to link is worse
than the flag being off. It also affects every C++ title here rather than this
one header.

diff --git a/include/toml++/impl/forward_declarations.hpp b/include/toml++/impl/forward_declarations.hpp
index 386a9e0..97d01f3 100644
--- a/include/toml++/impl/forward_declarations.hpp
+++ b/include/toml++/impl/forward_declarations.hpp
@@ -401,8 +401,12 @@ TOML_IMPL_NAMESPACE_START
 	inline constexpr bool is_cvref = std::is_reference_v<T> || std::is_const_v<T> || std::is_volatile_v<T>;
 
 	template <typename T>
+#if TOML_ENABLE_WINDOWS_COMPAT
 	inline constexpr bool is_wide_string =
 		is_one_of<std::decay_t<T>, const wchar_t*, wchar_t*, std::wstring_view, std::wstring>;
+#else
+	inline constexpr bool is_wide_string = false;
+#endif
 
 	template <typename T>
 	inline constexpr bool value_retrieval_is_nothrow = !std::is_same_v<remove_cvref<T>, std::string>
